A||N||4||Bill Shenefelt||Headlight relay on 87-down, not up-oone side only||||1||
Z||000000||Bill Shenefelt||12-31-2001||09:37 AM||||I had posted on the Mall in error, sorry. From what I have read on the forum it sounds like a relay problem. I have replaced the motor(new from Fiero store) but the drivers side goes down but not up. Passenger side works just fine. I saw that the relay control unit for an 87 is about $150! She already blew $130 for the motor so I don't want to just keep throwing money(hers) at it. Is it possible that the unit has only one bad internal relay that I can fix or replace just this part for a reasonable cost. How about a cross body wire to run both from the same relay output? I do have some parts from 84 to 86 like a relay I could wire as an actuator relay from the other side relay if necessary. Kind of hard to play with it though (by appointment only-my daughters 87, and she is usually not available)so I need to really have some sort of solution or real target in hand. <P>------------------<BR>Bill Shenefelt||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||12-31-2001||05:43 PM||||Try digging in salvage yards for 87+ sunbirds and maybe trans ams. Sunbird had that little half door on it. They use the same controller and motors. The sunbird controller I saw is up on the left shock tower easy to get at. (In other cars. If the motors look/wire the same as yours, then the controller should also be the same. GM likes to keep inventory down on this kind of thing. Take the dead one with you.)<P>I've heard the controller can be serviced but it's not made to be that way. It was meant to be a sealed part. I have no details on fixing it.<P>you can't run both motors on one circuit but if you CAREFULLY make an extension you could use one circuit to test the other motor. Just make sure the 2 wires can't short or you'll find out how bad fuse links smell when they burn.<P>If you do that then stay clear of the motor and lift.... if you hook it up backwards, it won't hurt anything but the motor will raise when it should go down and you don't want to get caught by it....<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||SKIDMARK||12-31-2001||06:08 PM||||Ogre, all those warnings sound like the voice of experience. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> If the relay system is similar to the 84-86, it could be the relay mounted on the headlight frame. I know the motors are different on the 87/88 but I think all the realys are the same. I had the same problem with my 86SE. If I tapped on the relay, the light would go up sometimes. A $15 replacement relay from the local parts store and everything is good as new.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||01-01-2002||07:07 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SKIDMARK:<BR><B>Ogre, all those warnings sound like the voice of experience.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> If the relay system is similar to the 84-86, it could be the relay mounted on the headlight frame. I know the motors are different on the 87/88 but I think all the realys are the same. I had the same problem with my 86SE. If I tapped on the relay, the light would go up sometimes. A $15 replacement relay from the local parts store and everything is good as new.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>The systems are alltogether different on the 87 & 88 headlight system when compareing to previous years. The problem is most definitaly with the relay. I have repaired them in the past depending on the damage inside. You should be able to get one at the wrecking yard in your area for less than $15.00, and the TA's DO use the same relay as well. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bill Shenefelt||01-01-2002||07:17 AM||||Thanks for the info about junk yard replacements.  I will try to get out tomorrow and search for one.  Great way to use up my vacation.  Oh well, gotta keep the kids car looking good.<BR>Thanks again for the help<P>------------------<BR>Bill Shenefelt||||reg||1
